# ⚠️ The repository had no `.gitattributes` and `core.autocrlf` is not something a
# clone can be relied on to set, so files landed in whatever ending the editor that
# created them used. The tree was genuinely mixed — thirteen CRLF files in the
# Rust shell of the time alone — and a formatter touching one rewrote every line of it: the
# review branch showed `spaces/store.rs` as +136/-129 for a real change of +28/-21,
# and `language.rs` as +546/-546 for +9/-9. A diff nobody can read is a diff nobody
# reviews.
#
# LF in the repository, whatever the working tree does. `text=auto` still lets Git
# check out CRLF where a platform asks for it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalized, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
